* Hyperliquid HIPs in twelve cards
** Execution layer
*** HyperCore\n//the exchange is the state machine//
*** Add Liquidity Only (ALO)\n//rest as maker or be rejected//
** Spot tokens and liquidity
*** HIP-1 token\n//capped supply, native book, identify by index not ticker//
*** Deployment Dutch auction\n//31 hours, falling price, 500 HYPE floor, paid once//
*** Hyperliquidity (HIP-2)\n//0.3% ladder, every 3 seconds, no operator, shared book//
** Builder perpetuals
*** Builder-deployed perp DEX (HIP-3)\n//500k HYPE stake, deployer runs oracle and risk//
*** Deployer slashing\n//irregular input → validator vote → stake burned, not refunded//
left side
** Outcome markets
*** Outcome (HIP-4)\n//Yes + No = 1 quote token, no leverage//
*** Split and merge\n//1 quote token ⇄ 1 Yes + 1 No//
*** Question\n//No on one = Yes on all the others//
*** Outcome template\n//validators approve the pattern, deployers fill the blanks//
** The proposals
*** Hyperliquid Improvement Proposal (HIP)\n//1 token, 2 liquidity, 3 perps, 4 outcomes//
